zone-groups:
  Under this point you have to define groups of world guard zones in which the plugin will check for broken blocks, and uses the loottable defined for this region.
  You can do this by giving it a name, for example: dirtArea.
  There are two subpoints for a group:
    - a settable flag "everywhere". If this flag is set to true, every block on the server is valid and will and the lootable defined for this area will be used
    - A map "region-ids", where you can list the world guard regions which will count to this region by adding them as a subpoint with "- <regionName>

global Flags:
  Here you can set global flags that generally count plugin wide.
    - "mutualy-exclusive-regions": if this is set to true, breaking a block will only check the loottable of the highest in the config defined zone-group where the block is a part of. Turing this flag off (or omitting it) is discouraged, since it may leed to unintended behaviour if multiple loottables try to spawn a container at the same location.
    - "deposit-to-inventory": if this flag is set to true, dropped Items and XP will instantely be depositied in the players inventory. If set false or it is omitted, the Items / Xp will drop at the location of the broken block.
    
